<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's sugar imports to rise 5.0 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Morocco's sugar imports to rise 5.0 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>CASABLANCA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's raw sugar imports are expected to total 500,000 tonnes in 1996, an increase of 5.0 percent over the previous year, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The import rise was due to a slight drop in domestic sugar output and a rise in consumption, they added.</p>
<p>Since January to November, Morocco purchased a total of 446,287 tonnes of raw sugar, mainly from south American and European markets, a trade ministry official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The state-owned Office National du The et du Sucre (ONTS) inmported nearly half of these quantities while the remaining tonnage was purchased by private importers,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
